# Local stack (Postgres + MinIO + Temporal) — connection + data-dir settings.
# Forge does NOT auto-load this file; export what you need in your shell
# (direnv/keychain or a manual `export`). Copy to `.env` only for the compose
# *_PORT / *_DATA overrides, which podman does read from this directory.
#
# ── Temporal ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# 0. Temporal self-hosts in this stack (production — D99), persisting to the
#    stack's Postgres. Workers and CLIs on the host connect via:
FORGE_TEMPORAL_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1:7233
PBOOK_TEMPORAL_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1:7233
#    Host ports (container-side stays 7233 / 8080). The UI defaults to 8233 —
#    same collision-avoidance convention as 5433/9002 below. UI at
#    http://localhost:8233.
# FORGE_TEMPORAL_PORT=7233
# FORGE_TEMPORAL_UI_PORT=8233
#
# ── Postgres ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# 1. FORGE_DB_URL — how the *app* (worker/CLI) connects. Forge does NOT
#    auto-load this file; export FORGE_DB_URL in your shell (direnv/keychain,
#    or a manual `export`) pointing at the container this compose file starts.
#    The credentials below are the throwaway literals baked into compose.yaml;
#    the port matches FORGE_PG_PORT's 5433 default (see below).
FORGE_DB_URL=postgresql+psycopg2://forge:forge@localhost:5433/forge_dev

# 2. FORGE_PG_PORT — host port the container publishes (container-side stays
#    5432). Defaults to 5433 so this coexists with another local Postgres
#    already on 5432 (e.g. a sibling project's dev DB). Override only if 5433 is
#    also taken; then point FORGE_DB_URL above at the same port.
# FORGE_PG_PORT=5434

# 3. FORGE_PG_DATA — host directory for the Postgres data volume, read by
#    compose. `make db-up` sets this to $XDG_DATA_HOME/forge/postgres for you,
#    so you only need it when running `podman compose` directly. Copy this
#    file to `.env` (in this directory) and uncomment to override; the
#    compose-side fallback is ./data/postgres beside compose.yaml.
# FORGE_PG_DATA=/absolute/path/to/pgdata

# ── Object storage (MinIO, S3-compatible) ───────────────────────────────────
#
# Forge's blob path uses boto3 against FORGE_OCR_S3_BUCKET. Point boto3 at the
# local MinIO with these four AWS_* vars: botocore honors AWS_ENDPOINT_URL_S3
# and uses path-style addressing, so `boto3.client("s3")` reaches MinIO with NO
# Forge code change. `make db-up` creates the bucket named below.
#
# FOOTGUN: these OVERRIDE any real-AWS creds/endpoint in your shell (same shape
# as FORGE_DB_URL → Supabase). Set all four together so you don't half-point at
# real S3. The port must match FORGE_MINIO_PORT (default 9002) below.
AWS_ENDPOINT_URL_S3=http://localhost:9002
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=forge
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=forge-minio-secret
AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=us-east-2
FORGE_OCR_S3_BUCKET=saxcapital-forge-blobs-dev

# 4. FORGE_MINIO_PORT / FORGE_MINIO_CONSOLE_PORT — host ports MinIO publishes
#    (container-side stays 9000/9001). Default 9002/9003 so this coexists with
#    a sibling project's MinIO already on 9000. Console UI is at
#    http://localhost:<console-port> (log in with the creds above). Override
#    only if 9002/9003 are also taken, and match AWS_ENDPOINT_URL_S3.
# FORGE_MINIO_PORT=9002
# FORGE_MINIO_CONSOLE_PORT=9003

# 5. FORGE_MINIO_DATA — host directory for the MinIO data volume (like
#    FORGE_PG_DATA; `make db-up` sets it to $XDG_DATA_HOME/forge/minio).
# FORGE_MINIO_DATA=/absolute/path/to/miniodata
